  'odds.implied': 'Implied odds: your equity is a little short, but stacks are deep (about {x}× the call), so when you hit you can win more later. Hidden hands (sets, straights) do best.',
  'odds.allin': 'This is an all-in call: no more decisions, so compare your equity with the {need} needed and nothing else.',
  'odds.free': 'No bet to you: you can see the next card for free. Check weak hands; bet with strong hands or a reason to bluff.',
  'spr.low': 'SPR (stack ÷ pot) is only {x}: little behind compared with the pot, so with top pair or better you are usually committed to the end.',
  'spr.mid': 'SPR is {x}: careful with one pair, happy to build a big pot with two pair or better.',
  'spr.high': 'SPR is {x} (deep): one pair is risky in a big pot. Strong hands (sets, straights) and draws gain value.',
  'fl.calls': 'In fixed limit the bets are small compared with the pot, so the price of a call is low — draws and medium pairs can call more often.',
  'opp.multi': '{n} opponents still in: someone is more likely to have a strong hand, so top pair is worth less and bluffs work less often.',
  'opp.hu': 'Heads-up: your opponent often has nothing much either; bets take the pot more often and one pair is worth more.',
  'act.allin': 'Your opponent is all-in: the range is weighted to strong hands (or big draws). Compare with the equity needed: do you beat their strong hands?',
  'act.big': 'A big bet ({x} of the pot) is usually polarized: very strong or a bluff. Medium hands are in a tough spot.',
