  'draw.oe': 'An open-ended straight draw: {n} outs × {k} ≈ {p}%. Either end completes it.',
  'draw.gs': 'A gutshot: {n} outs × {k} ≈ {p}%. Weak alone — continue only when the odds fit.',
  'draw.bd': 'A backdoor flush draw (two more of the suit): weak alone but adds a few percent of equity.',
  'draw.two': 'The flop “×4” assumes you see two cards; for the next card only use ×2. Bets may stop you seeing both.',
  'draw.dirty': 'Some outs are “dirty”: your straight could still lose to a flush or a full house — count your chances a little lower.',
  'river.call': 'The river: no more cards, equity is just “do I win now”. Is the bet value, or a missed draw bluffing?',
